---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';

const updated = new Date(site.privacyUpdated).toLocaleDateString('en-AU', {
  day: 'numeric',
  month: 'long',
  year: 'numeric',
});
const tel = site.phone.replace(/\s/g, '');
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy policy"
  description={`How ${site.name} collects, uses, stores and discloses your personal information, in line with the Australian Privacy Principles.`}
>
  <section class="head">
    <div class="shell">
      <span class="eyebrow">Legal</span>
      <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        This policy explains what personal information {site.name} collects when you request a quote or order a
        print, why we collect it, who we share it with and how you can access or correct it.
      </p>
      <p class="meta">Last updated {updated}</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="shell prose">
      <h2 id="who-we-are">1. Who we are</h2>
      <p>
        {site.legalName}{site.abn ? ` (ABN ${site.abn})` : ''} (“we”, “us”, “our”) is a 3D printing and 3D
        modelling business based in {site.location}. We can be reached at
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or <a href={`tel:${tel}`}>{site.phone}</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        We are committed to protecting your privacy and handling your personal information in accordance with the
        <em>Privacy Act 1988</em> (Cth) and the thirteen Australian Privacy Principles (APPs). As a small business
        operator we may not currently be bound by the Privacy Act, but we have chosen to follow the APPs as a
        matter of good practice. In this policy, “personal information” has the meaning given to it in the Privacy
        Act.
      </p>

      <h2 id="what-we-collect">2. What personal information we collect</h2>
      <p>We only collect information we reasonably need to quote on, produce and deliver your job. That usually means:</p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li><strong>Contact details</strong> — your name, email address, phone number and, where relevant, your business or organisation name.</li>
        <li><strong>Delivery details</strong> — the postal address you want your prints sent to.</li>
        <li><strong>Job details</strong> — the 3D files you send us (STL, 3MF, OBJ, STEP and similar), drawings, sketches, reference photos, dimensions, materials, colours, quantities, deadlines and any notes you include with your enquiry.</li>
        <li><strong>Correspondence</strong> — emails, messages and call notes exchanged with you about a quote or order.</li>
        <li><strong>Transaction records</strong> — what you ordered, what you were charged, and when it was paid. We do not collect or store your full credit card or bank details; payments are handled by our payment provider or by direct bank transfer.</li>
        <li><strong>Technical information</strong> — limited information your browser sends when you visit this site, such as your IP address, browser type and the pages you viewed.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not seek sensitive information (such as health, biometric or government identifier information) and
        ask that you do not send it to us. If you send us sensitive information anyway, we will treat it in
        accordance with this policy and delete it once it is no longer needed.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can deal with us anonymously or under a pseudonym when making a general enquiry. We cannot, however,
        quote accurately, take payment or ship a physical order without your name, contact and delivery details.
      </p>

      <h2 id="how-we-collect">3. How we collect it</h2>
      <p>We collect personal information directly from you when you:</p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>submit the quote form on our enquire page;</li>
        <li>email, phone or message us, including through social media;</li>
        <li>place an order, pay an invoice or arrange delivery or pickup; or</li>
        <li>send us files, models or reference material for a job.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We may also collect information from third parties where you have asked them to deal with us on your
        behalf, or from a shipping carrier in relation to a delivery. If we ever receive personal information
        about you that we did not ask for and do not need, we will destroy or de-identify it where the law allows.
      </p>

      <h2 id="why-we-collect">4. Why we collect and use it</h2>
      <p>We use your personal information to:</p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>prepare and send you a quote;</li>
        <li>print, model, finish, package and deliver your job;</li>
        <li>invoice you and process payment;</li>
        <li>communicate with you about your enquiry, order or a warranty or reprint issue;</li>
        <li>keep business and tax records required by Australian law;</li>
        <li>improve our services, pricing and this website; and</li>
        <li>meet our legal obligations.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We will not use or disclose your personal information for any other purpose unless you would reasonably
        expect it, you have consented, or we are required or authorised by law to do so.
      </p>

      <h2 id="your-files">5. Your 3D files and designs</h2>
      <p>
        We treat the files and designs you send us as confidential and as your property. We use them only to quote
        on and produce your job. We do not sell, licence, publish or reprint your models for anyone else, and we
        do not share them with other customers.
      </p>
      <p>
        We will not display photographs of your prints on this website, on social media or in any other marketing
        without your permission. If you would prefer your job stayed private, tell us and we will note it on your
        file.
      </p>

      <h2 id="disclosure">6. Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>We disclose personal information only where it is necessary to run our business. That may include:</p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li><strong>Form and email providers</strong> — our quote form is hosted by Fillout, and enquiries reach us by email, so information you submit passes through and is stored on their systems.</li>
        <li><strong>Shipping and delivery partners</strong> — Australia Post, Sendle and any courier we use, so that they can deliver your order.</li>
        <li><strong>Payment and accounting providers</strong> — our payment processor, bank and accounting software, to take payment and keep records.</li>
        <li><strong>Specialist contractors</strong> — occasionally we engage another printer or finisher to complete part of a job. They receive only what they need to do that work and are required to keep it confidential.</li>
        <li><strong>Professional advisers and authorities</strong> — our accountant, insurer or lawyer, and any court, regulator or law enforcement body where we are required or authorised by law to disclose.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>We do not sell, rent or trade your personal information.</p>

      <h2 id="overseas">7. Overseas disclosure</h2>
      <p>
        Some of the service providers we rely on — including our form provider and email and cloud storage
        services — store data on servers outside Australia, most commonly in the United States. By sending us an
        enquiry you consent to your information being stored and processed overseas by those providers.
      </p>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to use reputable providers that protect personal information to a standard
        comparable to the APPs. You should be aware that overseas recipients may not be subject to the Privacy
        Act, and that you may not be able to seek redress under the Act in relation to them.
      </p>

      <h2 id="cookies">8. Cookies and website analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This website does not set advertising or tracking cookies of its own. Our embedded quote form may set
        cookies that are necessary for the form to work, and our hosting provider keeps standard server logs
        (including IP addresses) for security and troubleshooting.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can block or delete cookies through your browser settings. Doing so may stop the quote form from
        working properly.
      </p>

      <h2 id="marketing">9. Direct marketing</h2>
      <p>
        We may occasionally email past and current customers about our services. Every marketing message we send
        will identify us and include an easy way to unsubscribe, as required by the <em>Spam Act 2003</em> (Cth).
        You can also opt out at any time by emailing <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. Opting out
        will not affect messages we need to send you about a current quote or order.
      </p>

      <h2 id="security">10. Security and retention</h2>
      <p>
        We take reasonable steps to protect your personal information from misuse, interference, loss and
        unauthorised access, modification or disclosure. Those steps include password-protected and access-limited
        devices and accounts, reputable service providers, and limiting who can see customer files.
      </p>
      <p>
        No method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and we cannot guarantee absolute security of
        information sent to us over the internet.
      </p>
      <p>
        We keep your information only as long as we need it. Financial and transaction records are kept for at
        least seven years as required by Australian tax law. Quote files and 3D models are generally kept while
        there is an active or reasonably expected job, so we can reprint or adjust a part for you, and are deleted
        or de-identified on request or once they are no longer needed.
      </p>

      <h2 id="breaches">11. Data breaches</h2>
      <p>
        If we become aware of a data breach that is likely to result in serious harm to anyone whose information
        we hold, we will assess it promptly and, where the Notifiable Data Breaches scheme applies, notify the
        affected individuals and the Office of the Australian Information Commissioner (OAIC).
      </p>

      <h2 id="access">12. Accessing and correcting your information</h2>
      <p>
        You may ask us for a copy of the personal information we hold about you, or ask us to correct it if it is
        inaccurate, out of date, incomplete, irrelevant or misleading. Email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we will respond within a reasonable time, normally
        within 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        We may need to verify your identity before releasing information. We do not charge for making a request,
        though we may charge a reasonable fee for the time and cost of supplying a large amount of information. If
        we refuse a request, we will tell you why in writing and explain how to complain.
      </p>
      <p>
        You can also ask us to delete your information. We will do so unless we are required to keep it by law,
        such as for tax records, or need it for a current job or an actual or potential dispute.
      </p>

      <h2 id="complaints">13. Complaints</h2>
      <p>
        If you think we have breached the Australian Privacy Principles or mishandled your personal information,
        please contact us first at <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with the details. We will
        acknowledge your complaint, investigate it and respond in writing, normally within 30 days.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you are not satisfied with our response, you can refer the matter to the Office of the Australian
        Information Commissioner:
      </p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>Website: <a href="https://www.oaic.gov.au" rel="noopener">www.oaic.gov.au</a></li>
        <li>Phone: 1300 363 992</li>
        <li>Post: GPO Box 5288, Sydney NSW 2001</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="changes">14. Changes to this policy</h2>
      <p>
        We may update this policy from time to time to reflect changes in our practices or the law. The current
        version will always be available on this page, with the date it took effect shown at the top. Significant
        changes will be brought to your attention where practical.
      </p>

      <h2 id="contact">15. Contact us</h2>
      <p>
        For any question about this policy or your personal information, contact
        {' '}{site.legalName}:
      </p>
      <ul class="bullets">
        <li>Email: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></li>
        <li>Phone: <a href={`tel:${tel}`}>{site.phone}</a></li>
        <li>Location: {site.location}</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .head {
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border);
    padding-bottom: 1.75rem;
  }

  .meta {
    margin-top: 0.75rem;
    font-size: 0.8rem;
    color: var(--text-dim);
  }

  .prose {
    max-width: 68ch;
  }

  .prose h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    scroll-margin-top: 1rem;
  }

  .prose h2:first-child {
    margin-top: 0;
  }

  .prose p {
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .prose a {
    color: var(--accent);
    overflow-wrap: break-word;
  }

  .prose strong {
    color: var(--text);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .bullets {
    margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    padding-left: 1.1rem;
    list-style: disc;
    color: var(--text-muted);
  }

  .bullets li {
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
</style>
